 "short_name": "Buffalo City",
 "_doc": "BCMM (MIDAS-family ledger, same engine as Emfuleni/Mbombela but with NO service headings). One flat charge ledger: ChargeDate / Service / Details / Charge(excl VAT) / VAT / Charge(incl VAT), every amount prefixed 'R'. Sections are therefore synthesised from the charge lines themselves (FIRE LEVY -> sundry, STANDARD REFUSE -> refuse, electricity meter line -> electricity, water meter line -> water, dated SEWERAGE COMMERCIAL line -> sewerage), in ledger order. THREE FILE SHAPES in the Telkom Buffalo City set, all handled: (A1) old masthead 'BUFFALO CITY METROPOLITAN MUNICIPALITY ... www.buffalocity.gov.za', Statement Date as YYYY/MM/DD, 'Due Date for payment', compact ledger, meter blocks written 'METER-NO <n> TARIFF: ELECTRICITY LARGE PO' / 'Curr = x Prev = y Cons = z' / 'Reading dates: Curr .. Prev ..' / '<n>.000 kWh', no Notified Max Demand; these files are also wrapped by a mailer control line '<![number removed]|[address removed]|...!>' at the top of every page - the full bill body sits underneath unchanged, so they are matched normally, not rejected. (A2) new masthead 'TAX INVOICE / BCMM VAT Registration No. 4240193492', Statement Date as DD/MM/YYYY, 'Due Date', blank-line-spaced ledger, but STILL the old METER-NO wording. (B) new masthead plus new meter wording 'METER NUMBER: <n>' / 'TARIFF: EL0300 ELECTRICITY LARGE POWER U' / 'READING DATES: Curr .. Prev ..' / 'READINGS: Curr .. Prev ..' / 'CONSUMPTION: <n>.000 kWh', and 'Demand = d Notified Max Demand = 0'; some of these carry a '[address removed]' sender line at the top. Every meter/reading/consumption rule carries both wordings as 'patterns' fallbacks with identical group order. ELECTRICITY IS TWO REGISTERS OF ONE PHYSICAL METER: [number removed] (kWh energy) and [number removed]K (kVa demand), plus a separate 'ELECTRICITY BASIC CHARGE LARGE POWER USER SCALE 3A' line. block_anchor was deliberately NOT used: it would emit two rows per bill (one kWh-only, one kVa-only) and orphan the basic charge, which is wrong for the one-row-per-meter canonical template. Instead each register has its own collect:'sum' rule and the row is assembled by computes - the proven path used by every shipped profile. Water uses the identical block shape ('TARIFF: WA0200 WATER COMMERCIAL BULK' / 'INTERIM 100.000 Kl'); the kWh/kVa/Kl unit words plus section scoping keep water out of every electricity column. IDENTITY / RULE ZERO: the bill prints NO independent ex-VAT electricity subtotal, so buf_elec_ex_r is the sum of its own three parts and the harness reconcile on this profile is structurally circular - stated plainly in the report. Two genuinely independent printed identities are used instead: (1) 'TOTAL CURRENT LEVY' is the INCL-VAT sum of the current-period charge lines ONLY (it excludes the SUB TOTAL brought-forward residue) - e.g. 24/05/26 bill: levy 192368.16, Total Charge (incl. VAT) 192297.36, SUB TOTAL -70.80, and 192368.16 - 70.80 = 192297.36 exactly; that is the whole 192368.16 vs 192297.36 discrepancy. (2) end reading minus start reading equals the printed kWh consumption, and printed VAT equals 15% of printed ex-VAT on every charge line.",
